{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 97b675b4: option B, and this amends S4's scope (a7d77a9b).\n\nA question names the Brief it was asked under, in the record. Option A would keep that fact in an operator-trusted table outside the record, so a reader could not check it from the room alone.\n\n1. Add one opt-in definition derived from S3, with one required ask field, brief, in the existing digest form, stored on the ask. S3's bytes and pin stay in place, and existing questions read as unbound. Act names and the bodyAt and person-only approval rules do not change. This head adds that definition to S4's reads and view.\n2. The Brief is immutable for the life of a question. revise-ask cannot change it, and a different Brief needs a new question. An approval names its text version, so a fixed Brief needs no second version binding.\n3. Serve the Brief as a text/plain resource at dap://package/brief, with exact raw UTF-8 bytes checked by digestBytes, bounded at 64 KiB. Keep the ui:// HTML rules as they are. Add no generic URI loader, external fetch, executable package body or fallback to the body digest.\n4. The pin grants no authority. Approving a question does not approve the Brief or the conditions.\n5. Add one witness: revise-ask with a different brief is refused. The plan's digest witness then stands as written.\n\nSay in the head's note whether the definition touches the kernel, so the checker can apply the filing gate.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:97b675b46d62557842b0590378deef6f382bb0a1 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}